<title>FRANCE: Paris airports import traffic up 1.1pct Jan-Oct.</title>
<headline>Paris airports import traffic up 1.1pct Jan-Oct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-October 1996 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 428,521 tonnes, an increase of 1.1 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>ADP import traffic, by region, with percentage change on January-October 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p>  Domestic		 24,986     down 12.5pct</p>
<p>  European Union	 51,600     up    7.0</p>
<p>  Non-EU Europe	   9,282     up    3.7</p>
<p>  North Africa	    8,382     down 11.4</p>
<p>  Sub-Saharan Africa   43,378     up    9.3</p>
<p>  North America	 150,974     up    2.6</p>
<p>  French territories   10,217     down  4.0</p>
<p>  Latin America	  15,032     down  6.3</p>
<p>  Middle East	    19,940     down  4.8</p>
<p>  Far East		 94,730     up    0.3</p>
<p>  Total		   428,521 tns up    1.1</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
